<p>Finally got it and it's&#8230; fine?</p>
<p>Like, the combat is kinda wonky and often feels tedious, and that makes the lack of any difficulty setting frustrating. (It's reasonable, but, like, just a smidge above what I would personally choose.)</p>
<p>The plot is ok and has some interesting ideas, but the style and tone feel kinda&#8230; samey, throughout. The weirdness isn't ever mind-blowing and it hasn't scared me yet. Like, the story and concepts are staying firmly in their own lanes/within the bounds of reasonability for what is already set up.</p>
<p>The <span style="background-color:black;"><span style="color:black">thresholds and astral plane</span></span> are cool but I wish they didn't all have muted color palettes.</p>
<p>Maybe I'm just spoiled by the wiki, or &quot;in a mood&quot; unrelated to the game, both have influenced me in the past.</p>
<p>Edit: Beat the main story. <span style="background-color:black;"><span style="color:black">Dyna-mite</span></span> fucking got me. That's some good weirdness.</p>

