<p>Ok, was wondering when someone would talk about the game. The Federal Bureau of Control actually feels like the UIU crossed with the Foundation, considering that they have &quot;containment procedures&quot; and a &quot;anonymous, and monolitic overseeing Board&quot;. One of the differences between the FBC and the SCP is that they already (as the game indicates) have an idea of what may cause these &quot;altered items&quot;, &quot;objects of power&quot;, &quot;places of power&quot; etc. etc., but the Foundation doesn't have that overarching idea and/or theory of what causes the anomalies.</p>
<p>Another thing, what if the Foundation found an entryway to &quot;The Oldest House&quot;, like they notice the building, but not anyone else, and when they enter to establish a base or establish containment, they find a similar anomalous group. Would the Foundation work with the FBC, or would it spark a rivalry?</p>
<p>These are the questions that interest me, especially since I could see both the FBC, UIU, and SCP all working to prevent the Hiss from escaping, while working on improving containment procedures.</p>

