			<div class="content" id="post-content-4775825">
									

<blockquote>
<p>One of the differences between the FBC and the SCP is that they already (as the game indicates) have an idea of what may cause these&#8230;</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Yeah, one of the differences I can see in the FBC-verse is that there's only &quot;one kind of magic.&quot; Everything that's altered has some kind of extradimensional influence leaking in. Major spoilers:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The Board are in/from the Astral Plane, the Hiss came from the projector (and so did Polaris, kinda. Jesse is a weird case.), blackrock comes from the quarry, the hotel is its own place, the fridge is really caused by the Former, etc etc.) It's true that people like Jesse have psychic powers, but even the Director Candidates are selected for the ability to Control objects of power.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
So it makes sense that the FBC have a theory, because no matter how weird, there is a common link.
<p>Edit: putting the interaction stuff in a collapsible.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>If the FBC, UIU, and Foundation met, I imagine they'd have to have some kind of negotiations and tension, but let everyone do their own thing. Just like they do with the Pentagram and UIU.</p>
<p><strong>For how the Foundation sees the FBC</strong>: I think the Foundation would classify the FBC, Jesse, the Oldest House, and all the AWEs/items/objects as subparts of a single SCP that they'd really like to contain, but wouldn't be able to. (The Board, The House, and Jesse are all really powerful.)<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-420271-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-420271-1')">1</a></sup> Honestly I can also see the Foundation making a move on the Board or the House and getting their nose bloodied for it in response, just like what happened with the Library. Same thing with going after Jesse.</p>
<p>I think the Foundation might also make a deal for those nice little harnesses, and maybe deliberately turn over Alerted Items and AWE s that that feel very strongly fit SCP-####. Does it make the Kant Counter tick or the Blackstone resonator? If B, then is an SCP-####-C, call SCP-####-A (the FBC)</p>
<p>Edit: Side thought, I think it's really cool/unique that the FBC responds to AWEs by packing up big parts of the location and rebuilding them in the Oldest House. I imagine that's going to cause a lot of fun conflict/frustration in the Foundation. Like, imagine if every time a field agent goes out to investigate an <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/log-of-extranormal-events">Extranormal Event</a> and distribute amnestics, they find guys in suits packing the whole town onto railcars, and they have to argue over who's turf this is.</p>
<p><strong>For the FBC and the UIU</strong>: I think the cooperation between the UIU and the FBC would make a lot of sense, given that the current canon UIU had a lot of interaction with Ways and pocket dimensions and Type Blue personnel. That said, I think the FBC would be just as horrified that random people (including the UIU) use dimensional portals all the time as the Foundation would be horrified if their employees just all started using magic.</p>
<p><strong>How the FBC see the Foundation:</strong> The SCP Foundation and SCP objects would make perfect sense to the FBC: The Foundation and SCPs all get their power from extradimensional Swann-type entities who will create their own AWEs and Altered Items and even Objects of Power (amnestics, SRAs, huge Sites and unreasonable amounts of money) for their own amusement. Just like the Board or the House, except the weird extradimensional rules they follow instead of normal physics are the rules of <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/i-h-p-proposal">narrative</a>. Hell, the FBC already know about Alan Wake, so horror writers screwing the universe isn't even really a leap.</p>
</div>
